      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report on a case of perhexiline maleate-induced hepatitis secondary to a long-term administration of recommended daily dosages of 300 mg. The patient had a spectacular weight loss of 29 kg. He developed hepatitis, which subsided after drug withdrawal. Our electron-microscopic findings with the typical inclusion bodies and impaired hydroxylation capacity point to an underlying metabolic disorder as the pathogenetic mechanism."},
